{
  "format": 1,
  "title": "Blended-cement concrete: binder composition for C40/50",
  "notes": "Binder composition study for a C40/50 structural concrete with 400 kg/m³ total binder, water/binder ratio 0.42, 1780 kg/m³ aggregate (0/4 sand and 4/16 crushed limestone) and a fixed PCE superplasticiser dosage of 0.8 % of binder. The four binder components are dosed in kg/m³ and always add up to 400 kg/m³; the component limits are based on EN 206 practice and plant silo capacity; the design blends are rounded to whole kilograms for batching. Mixes are cast in a 60 L laboratory pan mixer, four per day, slump is read to the nearest 5 mm, and strength is the mean of three 150 mm cubes cured in water at 20 °C. The fresh concrete temperature is measured after mixing and recorded as an environmental factor.",
